      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MASt3R 3D Reconstruction — 2-Image Template\n\nHOW TO USE:\n1. On each Load Image node below, click 'choose file to upload' and pick a photo. Both photos must be of the SAME scene from DIFFERENT angles (e.g. step left/right between shots).\n2. Click 'Queue Prompt' (top-right).\n3. The reconstructed 3D scene (point cloud + camera frustums) appears in the Preview 3D node on the right.\n   - Drag = orbit, scroll = zoom, right-drag = pan.\n   - Each colored pyramid is one input camera's position.\n4. GLB file is also saved to ComfyUI's output folder for download.\n\nVRAM TIPS (8GB / RTX 4070):\n- image_size = 384 is the safe default. If you get OOM (out of memory) errors, drop to 256.\n- Stick with scenegraph_type = 'complete' for 2-4 images.\n\nFOR MORE IMAGES:\n- Easiest: set image_folder_path on the MASt3R 3D Reconstruction node to a folder you fill with photos, then right-click the Batch Images node → Bypass.\n- Or duplicate the Load Image + Batch Images pattern."
      ]
